Congratulations on making it to Minetown with only 2 XP.  Nice work.  I
agree that the Protection Run is a good training tool for working with
pets and avoiding hazards.  For your next trick, why not try to make it
the top level of Sokoban while still Level 1?  I recommend two cats or
dogs for bodyguards, just don't let your pets near the giant mimics as
they will be killed.  Are you _sure_ that Mandy (large cat or large
dog, I presume) can handle the guards?  If she attacks the Watch
Captain make sure that you are nearby to heal her and keep track of her
hp with your stethoscope.  The Watch Captains fight back with swords or
sabers.  Be careful!

Definitely save the wand of wishing for something that you definitely
need.  Anything that you wish for at this point could very likely be in
a shop or lying on the floor in the dungeon.  BTW, it might feel like
forever but eventually you'll get something from the wand if you just
keep zapping it.

Regarding daggers, I'm not sure but you will probably find it
inconvenient with a STR=7 to carry too many of them.   Watch your
burdened status.  I'd save the charging scroll.  If you find a
spellbook of create monster, you'll wish that you had kept the scroll
for something else.

Caveat: I tend to play very cautiously and if you're not too confident
either, then I'd recommend that you not be too hasty.

I don't know about the icebox.  Why not try to put something expendable
inside, or else wait for someone more savvy to answer?

